Our client is currently recruiting a Project Manager for Brand Development and Management of Community Recycling Network,
Requirements:
Have a bachelor’s degree in a science, engineering, or environmental management and technology subject, or equivalent;
Minimum eight (8) years’ relevant full-time postqualification working experience in waste reduction, waste recovery/recycling, waste facilities management, recycling contract management, environmental education or related environmental domain, among which at least three (3) years in supervisory level and at least three (3) year working experience in contract management on waste recovery/recycling;
Have met the language proficiency requirement of Level 3 (see Note) or above in Chinese Language and English Language in the Hong Kong Diploma of Secondary Education Examination (HKDSEE) or the Hong Kong Certificate of Education Examination (HKCEE), or equivalent
[Note: “Grade C” in Chinese Language and English Language (Syllabus B) in the HKCEE before 2007 are accepted administratively as comparable to “Level 3” in Chinese Language and English Language in the 2007 HKCEE and henceforth]; OR met the language proficiency requirements of ‘Level 2’ results in the two language papers (Use of Chinese and Use of English) in the CRE, or equivalent;
Have good command of spoken and written English and Chinese;
Have good planning and organisation skills;
Have good personality and inter-personal communication skills, self-motivation and ability to work independently;
Have experience and knowledge on spatial design and shop renovation that aligned the branding including reviewing shop drawings, supervising/ monitoring the site works, site inspection and defect checking;
Have experience and knowledge in managing, maintaining and building the brand; and
Preference may be given to candidates with experience in computer knowledge and applications (such as word processing in Chinese and English, spreadsheet and presentation software, etc.) or handling on public enquiries or complaints.
Duties:
To manage the contract and monitor the operation of the facilities of GREEN@COMMUNITY, including monitoring contractors’ compliance with contract requirements and vetting submissions of the facility operators;
To handle and respond to public enquiries and complaints concerning community recycling network and their related services/events/activities;
To oversee and liaise with the consultants on the branding and spatial design of GREEN@COMMUNITY to meet the operational standards and requirements;
To prepare and update promotional materials, information notes, guidelines, presentation materials and other necessary materials in relation to the community recycling network;
To liaise with all relevant stakeholders, including but not limited to different Government departments, contractors and property management office when managing the GREEN@COMMUNITY related contracts;
To handle spatial design of GREEN@COMMUNITY and prepare relevant guidelines to ensure brand development and consistency;
To supervise, train and coach new staff of the team for supporting daily operations and various initiatives of the facilities of GREEN@COMMUNITY; and
To undertake other duties pertaining to the work to be assigned.
Deadline: 7 Sep 2026
Interested parties, please send your resume in WORD format, stating current & expected salary and availability by clicking apply now.

