Computational Scientist Senior Computational Scientist ES OPER
Computational Scientist / Senior Computational Scientist (ES-OPER)
Working Location
Hong Kong
Job Category
Technical Division - Computation
Job Description
Design computational model experiments and analyze results for Numerical Weather Prediction (NWP), Chemical Transport Models (CTM) and source apportionment tools;
Construct and update emission inventories based on available datasets;
Incorporate data assimilation and statistical methods to enhance model accuracy;
Visualize model outputs interactively for evaluation of atmospheric conditions;
Operate various atmospheric model simulations for weather and air quality forecasting, analysis and related applications;
Support the development and deployment of weather and air quality-related products / projects;
Support routine operations of forecasting systems as well as the underlying HPC / IT infrastructures.
Requirements
Master degree of abve in Meteorology, Physics, Computer Science or related discipline plus 2 years of work experience; or Bachelor degree in the above disciplines plus 4 years of work experience;
Strong background in computer programming skills;
Experience with computational environments (Linux/Unix), computer languages (Python, Fortran, etc.), and plotting and analysis tools (Python libraries: Numpy, xarray, matplotlib/Pyviz etc.) usually used for atmospheric modelling. Knowledge of GIS, C++, JavaScript or databases would be preferable;
Good understanding of atmospheric dynamics, numerical weather prediction models (WRF, MPAS), chemical transport models (CMAQ, CAMX), emission inventory tools (SMOKE) or data assimilation would be an advantage;
Candidate with higher academic qualification and/or more related experience may be considered as Senior Computational Scientist;
Good logical thinking and analytical mind;
Eager to learn, responsive with a can-do attitude at work;
Willing to take up challenges;
Team player, proactive in idea sharing with good communication skills;
Good spoken and written Mandarin and/or English.
Basic Benefits
We offer competitive remuneration package including 5-day work and 15 days annual leave to the right candidate with excellent career advancement.
